rest.prompt:
Create a production sprite sheet for the EXISTING white desktop kitten Neko, reference image is the exact character identity. This is hand-drawn stepped pixel-art animation, not a new character or illustration. Transparent RGBA background. ONE sheet, EXACTLY 4 columns by 3 rows, 12 complete chronological drawings, evenly spaced, generous clear margins in every cell. No labels, grid, shadows, floor, hearts, symbols, scenery or watermark. All sprites same camera, same physical head size, white fur, charcoal pixel outline, gray under-chin/chest shading, pink tiny nose and inner ears, big black eyes with little square highlights, compact seated body, attached curled tail on viewer right. Preserve the reference head-to-body ratio. Exactly two ears, one head, connected neck/torso, four anatomical legs with hidden hind legs occluded, two front paws planted at an identical baseline. Do NOT copy the black background.
Action: priority RESTING IDLE, quiet affectionate presence. Draw the torso's subtle breathing with actual changing chest contour, NEVER scale/translate the entire kitten. Paws and haunches remain planted, head crown remains nearly level. The chest softly lifts then releases; ears and lids follow slightly later. Expressions must be legible across several connected drawings rather than a one-frame wink.
Reading order left to right then next row:
0 exact calm attentive reference sit with both eyes open;
1 first quiet inhale, chest gently fuller, relaxed open eyes;
2 inhale settles, soft upper eyelids and tiny content mouth;
3 lids lower smoothly to a warm half-close, shoulders easing;
4 eyes close into soft content arcs, tiny relaxed mouth, no extra face symbols;
5 hold the closed-eyed contentment with a slightly released chest and relaxed ears, same feet/head size;
6 begin eyelid reopen naturally, chest returning;
7 eyes half open, calm soft gaze, same support;
8 both eyes open, one ear subtly angles outward while the other stays attentive;
9 ear eases back, small curious-soft gaze with a tiny head inclination, body still planted;
10 head returns almost to the exact reference angle, both eyes clear;
11 exact same neutral pose and silhouette as drawing0 for a seamless loop.
The change is delicate but clearly drawn. Keep all 12 kittens at the SAME scale; no body wobble, no growing/shrinking head, no sliding paws, no detached tail/fragments, no cartoon motion marks. Thin hard pixel clusters rather than blurred illustration edges. All complete tails/ears/feet must fit each cell.
